  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>A spiro compound, or spirane, is a chemical compound, typically an organic compound, that presents a twisted structure of two or more rings (a ring system), in which 2 or 3 rings are linked together by one common atom.</p><p>Bicyclo compounds are a class of saturated compounds consisting of two fused rings, having two or more atoms in common,&nbsp;and that take the name of an open chain hydrocarbon containing the same total number of atoms.</p><p>Aromatic compounds are chemical compounds that consist of conjugated planar ring systems accompanied by delocalised pi-electron clouds in place of individual alternating double and single bonds.</p><p>Heterocyclic compounds are cyclic compounds with the ring containing carbon and other element, the component being oxygen, nitrogen and sulphur.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/9415cc7c-b300-46df-8265-b39738389c50-image.png\" style=\"width: 395px; height: 280px;\" /></p><p>The name of&nbsp;<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/f4ffae34-dbb3-413f-b89d-fde937e7b6fd-image.png\" style=\"width: 87px; height: 72px;\" />is tetrahydro furan. The name of&nbsp;<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/44828382-0287-4128-b67a-55bbda63aea7-image.png\" style=\"width: 77px; height: 70px;\" />&nbsp;is furan. The name of&nbsp;<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/7f793be5-5413-48ea-b2e9-22e210d2199f-image.png\" style=\"width: 121px; height: 51px;\" />&nbsp;is 2,2,4,4-tetramethylbicyclo[1.1.0]butane. The name of&nbsp;<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/23a89438-33ea-43ac-beca-75dbf77587f8-image.png\" style=\"width: 125px; height: 72px;\" />&nbsp;is 1,2,4,5-tetramethylspiro[2.2]pentane</p></blockquote>",
